ugh the public API.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation and tests visibly preserve group order, skip exhausted groups while taking one item from each nonempty group per round, and avoid mutating inputs; tests cover ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read solution.py and test_solution.py. Determine whether the implementation takes one item from each currently nonempty group in order per round until exhausted, preserves order within groups, and does not mutate input groups or collections. Determine whether the tests exercise the public API and cover ordinary, boundary, and empty inputs. Assess only code and test content visible in the files.\\\"}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; tree = ast.parse(Path(\\\\\\\"test_solution.py\\\\\\\").read_text()); assert sum(isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef) and n.name.startswith(\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\") for c in ast.walk(tree) if isinstance(c, ast.ClassDef) for n in c.body) >= 2'\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The named files are relative to the supplied task workspace; solution.py or test_solution.py may not exist yet and may be created.\\\",\\\"The requested unittest discovery command is interpreted literally as `python -m unittest discover -v`; the suite is assumed discoverable by that command.\\\",\\\"The phrase \u201cboundary inputs\u201d is interpreted to include groups of unequal lengths and singleton groups.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\"